# --- v1.34.0: automatic deploys ----------------------------------------
# The build now runs in Cloudflare from this repository, so anything that
# is generated must stay out of it, and a stray credential file must never
# be committable by accident.
.wrangler/
.dev.vars
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*
Thumbs.db

# --- v1.139.0: the strays the 08-09 audit found on disk ------------------
# Windows names a file it cannot overwrite with a "-1" suffix, and those
# copies were being committed and pushed: worker/src/index-1.ts and -2.ts in
# the store, public/sw-1.js here. A duplicate is never a source file. The
# suffixes are listed one by one rather than as a range because a glob would
# also swallow a real file called something-v2.ts.
*-1.ts
*-2.ts
*-3.ts
*-1.tsx
*-2.tsx
*-1.js
*-2.js
*-1.mjs
*-2.mjs
*-1.json
*-2.json
*-1.md
*-2.md

# Working notes this session writes into the folder - never part of the app.
Claude outputs/
deploy-log.txt
*.log

# The v1.38.0 leak. The signature vault is private R2; nothing real is served
# from here any more. The five 1x1 placeholders and the README stay tracked,
# by name, so stale cached HTML gets a transparent pixel instead of a 404.
#
# WHAT THIS RULE CANNOT DO (09-09 audit): git ignores by NAME, never by size.
# A real scan saved over ceo-sign.png matches the exception below and would be
# committed by the next `git add -A`. The size check lives in two places that
# CAN do it: tests/no-public-signatures.mjs (run by PUSH.bat before it
# commits) and .githooks/pre-commit (run by git itself, so a hand-typed
# commit is covered too). Do not read the exception below as protection.
public/signatures/*
!public/signatures/README.txt
!public/signatures/*-sign.png

# v1.148.0 - the pre-commit gate itself must be in the repo, or a fresh clone
# has no gate at all. PUSH.bat points git at it (core.hooksPath) every run.
!.githooks/
!.githooks/pre-commit
